  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Which of the following is equivalent to\n\n\\[\\sqrt{\\dfrac{x}{1-\\dfrac{x-1}{x}}}\\]\n\nwhen \\(x \\lt 0?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-x\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(x\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt{\\dfrac{x}{2}}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(x\\sqrt{-1}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2006-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The denominator simplifies: \\(1-\\dfrac{x-1}{x}=\\dfrac{x-(x-1)}{x}=\\dfrac{1}{x}.\\)\n\nSo the expression is \\(\\sqrt{\\dfrac{x}{\\frac{1}{x}}}=\\sqrt{x^2}=|x|.\\) Since \\(x \\lt 0,\\) this equals \\(-x.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Combine the denominator \\(1-\\dfrac{x-1}{x}\\) into a single fraction",
        "\\(\\sqrt{x^2}=|x|,\\) and \\(|x|=-x\\) when \\(x \\lt 0\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
